#: ../../maths/exotics.md:1 6ca29df6879343cab02f334b9a3a7b82
msgid "The exotic styles"
msgstr "新奇選擇權類型"

#: ../../maths/exotics.md:3 c66018a2d1604dd4a6c7dbb4d7d9c8f5
msgid "All nine exotic styles this build prices have closed forms inside the same Black-Scholes model — that is why each one's default engine is analytic rather than a grid. Each is a different set of boundary conditions on the same equation, and several are assembled out of the terms of the ones above them: the cliquet is a sum of forward starts, the knock digital is the barrier formula with a different payoff, and the one-touch is a single term of it."
msgstr "這個版本計價的九種新奇類型，在同一個 Black-Scholes 模型內都有封閉解——這也是每一種的預設引擎都是解析解而不是網格的原因。每一種都是同一個方程式上的一組不同邊界條件，而且好幾種是用前面那幾種的項組裝出來的：棘輪式是一連串遠期起始的加總，敲出入二元選擇權是換了收益函數的障礙公式，而 one-touch 就是那條公式裡的一項。"

#: ../../maths/exotics.md:10 bb5925f8d60845d9bacdc8959fef421e
msgid "Three of the nine also have a sampled engine, and none of the three is an approximation of a closed form for its own sake: the arithmetic-average Asian has no closed form at all, the performance cliquet's Monte Carlo engine is the only sampled cliquet engine QuantLib has, and a basket past two assets leaves the closed forms behind entirely."
msgstr "九種當中有三種另外還有抽樣型引擎，而三個都不是為了近似某條封閉解而近似：算術平均的亞式根本沒有封閉解，表現型棘輪式的蒙地卡羅引擎是 QuantLib 唯一的抽樣型棘輪引擎，而一籃子只要超過兩個資產就完全離開了封閉解的範圍。"

#: ../../maths/exotics.md:16 b2fca369671243fb8e29887ef3cf7183
#, python-brace-format
msgid "Throughout: $b = r - q$, $v = \\sigma\\sqrt{T}$, and"
msgstr "以下通用：$b = r - q$、$v = \\sigma\\sqrt{T}$，以及"

#: ../../maths/exotics.md:18 5e5c6003d9d74abe9edbd6621b1b48fd
msgid ""
"\\mu = \\frac{b - \\tfrac{1}{2}\\sigma^2}{\\sigma^2},\n"
"\\qquad\n"
"\\lambda = \\sqrt{\\mu^2 + \\frac{2r}{\\sigma^2}}."
msgstr ""

#: ../../maths/exotics.md:22 e9db8b3263434c0ba4cf332d8e673607
msgid "Barrier"
msgstr "障礙"

#: ../../maths/exotics.md:24 fe10e866ff344982a1058a525f877f3c
msgid "A barrier option is a vanilla that is switched on (*in*) or off (*out*) if the spot touches $H$ before expiry. The closed form is Merton (1973) and Reiner-Rubinstein (1991), and it is assembled from six terms. With $\\phi = \\pm 1$ for call/put and $\\eta = \\pm 1$ for down/up:"
msgstr "障礙選擇權是一檔一般型選擇權，在現貨於到期前觸及 $H$ 時被開啟（*入*）或關閉（*出*）。封閉解出自 Merton（1973）與 Reiner-Rubinstein（1991），由六項組合而成。其中買權／賣權為 $\\phi = \\pm 1$，下／上為 $\\eta = \\pm 1$："

#: ../../maths/exotics.md:29 3760621d0cd34a2ea1fa8e42f2e98623
#, python-brace-format
msgid ""
"x_1 = \\frac{\\ln(S/K)}{v} + (1+\\mu)v, \\qquad\n"
"x_2 = \\frac{\\ln(S/H)}{v} + (1+\\mu)v,"
msgstr ""

#: ../../maths/exotics.md:32 2877fed6fa4b4ead9c5e750cb159257f
msgid ""
"y_1 = \\frac{\\ln\\!\\big(H^2/(SK)\\big)}{v} + (1+\\mu)v, \\qquad\n"
"y_2 = \\frac{\\ln(H/S)}{v} + (1+\\mu)v, \\qquad\n"
"z = \\frac{\\ln(H/S)}{v} + \\lambda v,"
msgstr ""

#: ../../maths/exotics.md:36 3769cd2d29154977829c8ba05893eff2
#, python-brace-format
msgid ""
"\\begin{aligned}\n"
"A &= \\phi S D_q N(\\phi x_1) - \\phi K D_r N(\\phi x_1 - \\phi v),\\\\\n"
"B &= \\phi S D_q N(\\phi x_2) - \\phi K D_r N(\\phi x_2 - \\phi v),\\\\\n"
"C &= \\phi S D_q (H/S)^{2(\\mu+1)} N(\\eta y_1) - \\phi K D_r (H/S)^{2\\mu} N(\\eta y_1 - \\eta v),\\\\\n"
"D &= \\phi S D_q (H/S)^{2(\\mu+1)} N(\\eta y_2) - \\phi K D_r (H/S)^{2\\mu} N(\\eta y_2 - \\eta v),\\\\\n"
"E &= R\\,D_r\\big[N(\\eta x_2 - \\eta v) - (H/S)^{2\\mu} N(\\eta y_2 - \\eta v)\\big],\\\\\n"
"F &= R\\big[(H/S)^{\\mu+\\lambda} N(\\eta z) + (H/S)^{\\mu-\\lambda} N(\\eta z - 2\\eta\\lambda v)\\big],\n"
"\\end{aligned}"
msgstr ""

#: ../../maths/exotics.md:45 df7db4fe48d04b43b0747e6ad0e4ea32
msgid "where $R$ is the rebate. Each of the eight barrier types is a signed sum of these: a down-and-in call with $K > H$ is $C + E$; a down-and-out call with $K > H$ is $A - C + F$; and so on. $E$ is the rebate paid *at expiry*, $F$ the rebate paid *at hit*."
msgstr "其中 $R$ 是回饋金。八種障礙型式各是這些項的帶號和：$K > H$ 的下入買權是 $C + E$；$K > H$ 的下出買權是 $A - C + F$，其餘依此類推。$E$ 是*到期時*支付的回饋金，$F$ 是*觸及時*支付的回饋金。"

#: ../../maths/exotics.md:50 34924588243f4c48954edfe89bedf20f
msgid "Two properties are worth using as checks, and the service's own test suite uses both:"
msgstr "有兩項性質值得拿來當檢查，服務自己的測試套件兩者都用："

#: ../../maths/exotics.md:53 24e0d45ee4ef4448adf2bdea1d32e24c
msgid "V_{\\text{in}} + V_{\\text{out}} = V_{\\text{vanilla}} \\quad (R = 0),"
msgstr ""

#: ../../maths/exotics.md:55 9216dd9b0998464188360c9b251e43d9
msgid "and an unreachable barrier degrades to the vanilla price exactly."
msgstr "以及：一個永遠碰不到的障礙會恰好退化成一般型的價格。"

#: ../../maths/exotics.md:57 40f811b078154ba89d9ab720769423cf
msgid "**What is not built:** discrete monitoring and partial-time (window) barriers. The formula above assumes the barrier is monitored *continuously*, which is worth remembering when comparing against a contract that is monitored daily — continuous monitoring is worth strictly more knock-out protection, so the prices differ systematically rather than randomly."
msgstr "**沒有實作的部分**：離散觀察與部分期間（窗口）障礙。上面的公式假設障礙是*連續*觀察的，在與逐日觀察的合約比較時值得記住這一點——連續觀察提供的敲出保護嚴格更多，因此價格的差異是系統性的，而不是隨機的。"

#: ../../maths/exotics.md:63 bc9edbe1672242f5acc7ba1496a5fe55
msgid "Double barrier"
msgstr "雙障礙"

#: ../../maths/exotics.md:65 8b8464bcea7a479fa150303883ede07c
msgid "Two barriers, $0 < L < U$, both monitored continuously. The closed form is Ikeda-Kunitomo (1992): repeated reflection between the two levels produces an **infinite series of image terms**, each one a normal probability, converging geometrically. QuantLib truncates it; the truncation error is far below the tolerance you would price to."
msgstr "兩個障礙 $0 < L < U$，兩者都連續觀察。封閉解出自 Ikeda-Kunitomo（1992）：在兩個水準之間反覆反射，會產生一個**無窮的鏡像項級數**，每一項都是一個常態機率，並以幾何速度收斂。QuantLib 對它做截斷；截斷誤差遠低於你會用來計價的容忍度。"

#: ../../maths/exotics.md:71 7db0965d2d594dc68c7902edc2660a2c
msgid "There is no finite-difference route for this style in the build, because QuantLib's only FD double-barrier engine is a Heston engine and takes a calibrated model rather than a process."
msgstr "這個版本沒有為這個類型提供有限差分路徑，因為 QuantLib 唯一的有限差分雙障礙引擎是 Heston 引擎，它吃的是校準過的模型而不是隨機過程。"

#: ../../maths/exotics.md:75 a3a7547edc37418db2e90c559bf1eb6b
msgid "Asian"
msgstr "亞式"

#: ../../maths/exotics.md:77 48929a0b9a6a4a0ba16e1375db4cdf7a
msgid "An Asian option pays off against the **average** of the underlying rather than its terminal value. Whether there is a closed form depends entirely on which average."
msgstr "亞式選擇權的收益是對標的的**平均值**計算，而不是對它的期末值。有沒有封閉解，完全取決於是哪一種平均。"

#: ../../maths/exotics.md:81 482eb2ff9ea9464ab3cfc668942cd4d5
msgid "**Geometric, continuous.** The geometric average of a geometric Brownian motion is itself lognormal, so the option is a Black-Scholes option with adjusted parameters. QuantLib prices it as a Black formula with"
msgstr "**幾何平均、連續**。幾何布朗運動的幾何平均本身仍是對數常態，因此這檔選擇權就是一檔參數經過調整的 Black-Scholes 選擇權。QuantLib 以 Black 公式為它計價，其中"

#: ../../maths/exotics.md:85 15386754f71c406e98d3255eb5c57df4
msgid ""
"\\sigma_G = \\frac{\\sigma}{\\sqrt{3}},\n"
"\\qquad\n"
"q_G = \\frac{1}{2}\\left(r + q + \\frac{\\sigma^2}{6}\\right),"
msgstr ""

#: ../../maths/exotics.md:89 d3ce01f975bf4e2ea248e92be7543fdf
#, python-brace-format
msgid "the second being an effective dividend yield (`ql/pricingengines/asian/analytic_cont_geom_av_price.cpp`). The $1/\\sqrt{3}$ is the whole story of an Asian: averaging over the life of the option cuts the variance of the terminal quantity to a third, so an Asian is always worth less than the corresponding vanilla."
msgstr "第二式是一個等效股利收益率（`ql/pricingengines/asian/analytic_cont_geom_av_price.cpp`）。$1/\\sqrt{3}$ 就是亞式選擇權的整個故事：在選擇權存續期間取平均，把期末量的變異數削到三分之一，因此亞式永遠比對應的一般型便宜。"

#: ../../maths/exotics.md:95 031a0ec6c27c4e768d274c73abb1e42f
msgid "**Geometric, discrete.** With fixing dates the average is over a finite set, and $\\ln G$ is again normal — with mean and variance computed from the fixing times rather than from the closed-form limit. Same Black formula, different moments."
msgstr "**幾何平均、離散**。有定盤日時，平均是對有限個點取的，而 $\\ln G$ 仍為常態——只是均值與變異數由各定盤時點算出，而不是取連續極限的封閉式。同一個 Black 公式，不同的動差。"

#: ../../maths/exotics.md:100 7621af67ea744366b348ef150d97035d
msgid "**Arithmetic.** The sum of lognormals is not lognormal and there is no exact closed form, so this is the one style in the build that *must* go to Monte Carlo. QuantLib's engine can use the geometric average as a **control variate** — it is highly correlated with the arithmetic average and its value is known exactly, so subtracting its simulation error removes most of the noise. Turn it on when you have one; it is worth far more than the same time spent on extra paths."
msgstr "**算術平均**。對數常態之和不是對數常態，也沒有精確的封閉解，因此這是這個版本中唯一*必須*走蒙地卡羅的類型。QuantLib 的引擎可以用幾何平均當**控制變量**——它與算術平均高度相關，而且它的值是精確已知的，因此扣掉它的模擬誤差就能消掉大部分噪音。有得用就打開它；它的價值遠高於把同樣的時間拿去多跑路徑。"

#: ../../maths/exotics.md:108 3b459798f15546cbb1e47f777eb677c8
msgid "Lookback"
msgstr "回顧式"

#: ../../maths/exotics.md:110 47f73fb34c5e4c49addad4a0b0bfd1d7
msgid "A lookback pays off against the running extremum of the path, which must be supplied: an option already part-way through its life whose extremum is dropped would price as though it had just started."
msgstr "回顧式的收益是對路徑的累積極值計算，而該極值必須提供：一檔已經走了一段的選擇權若漏掉極值，會被當成剛剛才開始那樣計價。"

#: ../../maths/exotics.md:114 392c76b3777d479b854436460b3370ad
msgid "**Floating strike:** a call pays $S_T - m$, where $m$ is the running minimum."
msgstr "**浮動履約價**：買權支付 $S_T - m$，其中 $m$ 是累積最小值。"

#: ../../maths/exotics.md:115 8588c7292d294b3ab325a58b50c05888
msgid "**Fixed strike:** a call pays $\\max(M - K, 0)$, where $M$ is the running maximum."
msgstr "**固定履約價**：買權支付 $\\max(M - K, 0)$，其中 $M$ 是累積最大值。"

#: ../../maths/exotics.md:118 d58e4deb88964baf8855214ddff3aa9f
msgid "Both have closed forms under continuous monitoring — Goldman-Sosin-Gatto (1979) for the floating case, Conze-Viswanathan (1991) for the fixed. The floating call is"
msgstr "在連續觀察下兩者都有封閉解——浮動的情形是 Goldman-Sosin-Gatto（1979），固定的情形是 Conze-Viswanathan（1991）。浮動買權為"

#: ../../maths/exotics.md:122 01fbf9e3d2cf4371982a890a664a6423
msgid ""
"c = S D_q N(a_1) - m D_r N(a_2)\n"
" + S D_r \\frac{\\sigma^2}{2b}\\left[\\left(\\frac{S}{m}\\right)^{-2b/\\sigma^2} N\\!\\left(-a_1 + \\frac{2b\\sqrt{T}}{\\sigma}\\right) - e^{bT}N(-a_1)\\right],"
msgstr ""

#: ../../maths/exotics.md:125 852ec0c4a021423da9b3c8a0e75a0711
msgid ""
"a_1 = \\frac{\\ln(S/m) + (b + \\tfrac{1}{2}\\sigma^2)T}{\\sigma\\sqrt{T}},\n"
"\\qquad a_2 = a_1 - \\sigma\\sqrt{T}."
msgstr ""

#: ../../maths/exotics.md:128 b52a469d9e0d4565867765fa2515e652
msgid "The third term is the value of the *option to have done better* — the part that distinguishes a lookback from a vanilla struck at the extremum. Note it is singular as $b \\to 0$; the engine handles that limit, but it is why a lookback is unusually sensitive to the carry."
msgstr "第三項是*本來可以做得更好*這個選擇權的價值——正是它把回顧式和一檔以極值為履約價的一般型區分開來。注意它在 $b \\to 0$ 時是奇異的；引擎會處理那個極限，但這也是回顧式對持有成本異常敏感的原因。"

#: ../../maths/exotics.md:133 c2c0db6c6a78412b85a394168de0cc4d
msgid "Continuous monitoring again: a lookback priced against a daily-observed contract is an upper bound."
msgstr "同樣是連續觀察：拿來為逐日觀察的合約計價時，回顧式的價格是一個上界。"

#: ../../maths/exotics.md:136 514805dfd5ec498c8d359332e773fd92
msgid "Forward start"
msgstr "遠期起始"

#: ../../maths/exotics.md:138 5316b8cc963b43d5bb232d59cd688d37
#, python-brace-format
msgid "The strike is not known yet. It is set at the reset date $t_1$ to a multiple of the spot then, $K = m\\,S_{t_1}$, so the option's *moneyness* is fixed but its strike is not — which is why the trade carries no strike and a struck payoff would be silently overwritten."
msgstr "履約價目前還不知道。它會在重設日 $t_1$ 被設為當時現貨價的某個倍數 $K = m\\,S_{t_1}$，因此選擇權的*價內程度*是固定的，履約價卻不是——這也是為什麼這筆交易不帶履約價，而帶了履約價的收益函數會被無聲覆寫。"

#: ../../maths/exotics.md:143 984cd84993374107848da5baa0b91182
#, python-brace-format
msgid "Because the Black-Scholes price is homogeneous of degree one in $(S, K)$, the value at $t_1$ is $S_{t_1}$ times the value of a unit-spot option struck at $m$ over the remaining life $\\tau = T - t_1$. Discounting that back:"
msgstr "由於 Black-Scholes 價格對 $(S, K)$ 是一階齊次的，在 $t_1$ 時的價值等於 $S_{t_1}$ 乘上一檔「現貨為一單位、履約價為 $m$、剩餘期限 $\\tau = T - t_1$」的選擇權價值。再把它折現回來："

#: ../../maths/exotics.md:147 103638b21e194cfc85c776e0e365a9cf
msgid "V_0 = D_q(t_1)\\; S_0 \\; V_{\\text{BS}}\\big(1,\\ m,\\ \\tau\\big)."
msgstr ""

#: ../../maths/exotics.md:149 2ff22a0ac3d74a3fbfc4747d6ba014fa
msgid "QuantLib composes this literally: the forward engine prices the inner vanilla and multiplies by the dividend discount to the reset date (`ql/pricingengines/forward/forwardengine.hpp`)."
msgstr "QuantLib 就是照字面組合出來的：遠期引擎為內層的一般型計價，再乘上到重設日的股利折現因子（`ql/pricingengines/forward/forwardengine.hpp`）。"

#: ../../maths/exotics.md:153 5b972f8cc803468fbc11687d59927f0b
#, python-brace-format
msgid "The **performance** variant pays the *return* rather than the amount — it settles $\\max(S_T/S_{t_1} - m, 0)$ — so the payoff is already unit-scaled and the discount to the reset date is the risk-free one instead:"
msgstr "**performance** 變體支付的是*報酬率*而不是金額——它結算 $\\max(S_T/S_{t_1} - m, 0)$——因此收益已經是單位化的，到重設日的折現改用無風險折現因子："

#: ../../maths/exotics.md:157 c08e055a80324327be5a530bf81cf84b
msgid "V_0^{\\text{perf}} = D_r(t_1)\\; V_{\\text{BS}}\\big(1,\\ m,\\ \\tau\\big)."
msgstr ""

#: ../../maths/exotics.md:159 02e5007ee8a843a2a3d9161d8d60b03e
msgid "Same trade description, different price. The switch is on the style card."
msgstr "同一段交易描述，不同的價格。開關就在類型卡片上。"

#: ../../maths/exotics.md:161 d83138b8958942e8bd5e75584a2a9815
msgid "Cliquet"
msgstr "棘輪式"

#: ../../maths/exotics.md:163 953782805a28496e830edccdd46b0124
#, python-brace-format
msgid "A cliquet — a *ratchet* — is a series of forward starts laid end to end. Reset dates $t_1 < \\dots < t_{n-1}$ split the life into $n$ periods, the last ending at expiry, and each period is struck at $m$ times the spot when that period opens. So it is the section above, once per period:"
msgstr "棘輪式（cliquet，又稱 *ratchet*）是一連串首尾相接的遠期起始選擇權。重設日 $t_1 < \\dots < t_{n-1}$ 把存續期切成 $n$ 段，最後一段結束於到期日，而每一段的履約價都是該段開始時現貨價的 $m$ 倍。所以它就是上一節的東西，每一段來一次："

#: ../../maths/exotics.md:168 b9e1c49d2b9e4816b57c48cfc7c39c11
msgid ""
"V_0 = \\sum_{i=1}^{n} D_q(t_{i-1})\\; S_0\\; V_{\\text{BS}}\\big(1,\\ m,\\\n"
"t_i - t_{i-1}\\big), \\qquad t_0 = 0,\\ t_n = T."
msgstr ""

#: ../../maths/exotics.md:171 fae2157360314d45aeb22256ae3df938
msgid "QuantLib assembles it exactly that way — one Black calculation per period, at that period's forward and its *forward* variance, weighted by the dividend discount to the period's start (`analyticcliquetengine.cpp:70-84`) — and it appends the expiry to the reset list to close the final period. The **performance** form makes the same substitution the forward start does, discounting at the risk-free rate and paying the return:"
msgstr "QuantLib 就是照這樣組出來的——每一段做一次 Black 計算，用該段的遠期價與該段的*遠期*變異數，再乘上折現到該段起點的股利折現因子（`analyticcliquetengine.cpp:70-84`）——並且把到期日接在重設日清單後面，好把最後一段收尾。**表現型**做的是和遠期起始相同的替換：改用無風險利率折現，支付的是報酬率："

#: ../../maths/exotics.md:178 c08e055a80324327be5a530bf81cf84b
msgid ""
"V_0^{\\text{perf}} = \\sum_{i=1}^{n} D_r(t_{i-1})\\; V_{\\text{BS}}\\big(1,\\\n"
"m,\\ t_i - t_{i-1}\\big)."
msgstr ""

#: ../../maths/exotics.md:181 21e661c5b9d94bf4bbf748eb45d82250
msgid "**There are no caps or floors here, and that is a property of the library rather than of this page.** A capped cliquet truncates each period's return before summing, which is a different sum and not a scaling of this one. QuantLib's instrument carries the four fields and never passes them to an engine, so the price you would get is the uncapped sum above. The service refuses them by name rather than returning it."
msgstr "**這裡沒有上下限，而這是函式庫的性質，不是這一頁的性質**。帶上限的棘輪式會在加總之前把每一段的報酬率截斷，那是另一個總和，不是這個總和的縮放。QuantLib 的商品類別帶著那四個欄位，卻從來不把它們交給引擎，所以你拿到的價格會是上面那個沒有上限的總和。服務會指名拒絕它們，而不是把那個價格給你。"

#: ../../maths/exotics.md:188 27684c309639483980170c98cce8406b
msgid "Compound"
msgstr "複合式"

#: ../../maths/exotics.md:190 e48bade46dbe446a92374da914367a5e
msgid "An option on an option. The mother, struck at $K_1$ and expiring at $\\tau_1$, buys the daughter, struck at $K_2$ and expiring at $\\tau_2 > \\tau_1$."
msgstr "選擇權上的選擇權。母選擇權履約價 $K_1$、到期 $\\tau_1$，買到的是履約價 $K_2$、到期 $\\tau_2 > \\tau_1$ 的子選擇權。"

#: ../../maths/exotics.md:193 3d57b8b3a03a4a88ab0191b089e29d47
msgid "The whole difficulty is one number: the spot $S^*$ at which the mother is worth exercising, which is the spot at which the daughter is worth exactly what the mother costs,"
msgstr "全部的難處就在一個數字：讓母選擇權值得履約的那個現貨價 $S^*$，也就是子選擇權的價值恰好等於母選擇權履約成本的那個現貨價，"

#: ../../maths/exotics.md:197 d3cf5966137241ecae003de70a04c996
msgid "V_{\\text{daughter}}\\big(S^*,\\ K_2,\\ \\tau_2 - \\tau_1\\big) = K_1."
msgstr ""

#: ../../maths/exotics.md:199 4f7371cb761b46a19215e7777543785f
#, python-brace-format
msgid "That has no closed form, so QuantLib solves it with Brent (`analyticcompoundoptionengine.cpp:92-96`) and then the price is a Geske (1979) expression in two correlated normals — the daughter finishing in the money and the mother being exercised, correlated by $\\rho = \\sqrt{\\tau_1/\\tau_2}$ because the first period is contained in the second. With $\\phi = \\pm 1$ for a call or put daughter and $w = \\pm 1$ for a call or put mother, one expression covers all four combinations:"
msgstr "這個沒有封閉解，所以 QuantLib 用 Brent 法去解（`analyticcompoundoptionengine.cpp:92-96`），接著價格就是 Geske（1979）那個由兩個相關常態組成的式子——子選擇權到期在價內，以及母選擇權被履約，兩者的相關係數是 $\\rho = \\sqrt{\\tau_1/\\tau_2}$，因為第一段期間包含在第二段之內。以 $\\phi = \\pm 1$ 表示子選擇權是買權或賣權、$w = \\pm 1$ 表示母選擇權是買權或賣權，一個式子就涵蓋全部四種組合："

#: ../../maths/exotics.md:207 9b26d13f72704a98a4033712b01130c8
msgid ""
"V = \\phi w\\, S D_q(\\tau_2)\\, N_2\\!\\big(\\!-\\phi w X', \\phi d_+; w\\rho\\big)\n"
"\\; - \\; \\phi w\\, K_2 D_r(\\tau_2)\\, N_2\\!\\big(\\!-\\phi w X, \\phi d_-; w\\rho\\big)\n"
"\\; - \\; w\\, K_1 D_r(\\tau_1)\\, N\\!\\big(\\!-\\phi w X\\big),"
msgstr ""

#: ../../maths/exotics.md:211 d04d7644cb88450c996de1355621a4bb
#, python-brace-format
msgid "where $X$ is $S^*$ in the log-return coordinates Wystup uses, $X' = X - \\sigma\\sqrt{\\tau_1}$, and $d_\\pm$ are the usual daughter arguments at $\\tau_2$. Read it right to left: the last term is the premium paid, the middle one the strike paid on the daughter, the first the asset received."
msgstr "其中 $X$ 是 $S^*$ 換算到 Wystup 所用的對數報酬座標，$X' = X - \\sigma\\sqrt{\\tau_1}$，而 $d_\\pm$ 是子選擇權在 $\\tau_2$ 的那組常見引數。從右往左讀：最後一項是付出的權利金，中間一項是子選擇權上付出的履約價，第一項是收到的標的資產。"

#: ../../maths/exotics.md:216 c9648ef12a7c431c961509218a450fa4
msgid "**The compound must expire on or before the option it buys.** Not a modelling choice — there is nothing to exercise into otherwise, and QuantLib's instrument rejects it."
msgstr "**複合式的到期日必須不晚於它所買到的那個選擇權**。這不是模型上的選擇——否則履約之後根本沒有東西可換，而 QuantLib 的商品類別也會拒絕。"

#: ../../maths/exotics.md:220 bd4dc4dfe5324487826ace29f39cb4b1
msgid "Chooser"
msgstr "選擇者"

#: ../../maths/exotics.md:222 786ee879d1554567976ee2f4c7fd0831
msgid "The holder decides at $t_c$ whether the option is a call or a put. Until then it is neither, which is why the trade carries no option type at all."
msgstr "持有人在 $t_c$ 決定這是買權還是賣權。在那之前它兩者都不是，這就是為什麼這筆交易根本不帶選擇權型態。"

#: ../../maths/exotics.md:225 a425693de5be444aaa72794bc4402da1
msgid "**Simple chooser** — one strike $K$, one expiry $T$ for both sides. At $t_c$ the holder takes $\\max(c, p)$, and put-call parity turns that into a call plus a put on the *forward*, giving a closed form in two univariate normals (`analyticsimplechooserengine.cpp:74-87`):"
msgstr "**簡單選擇者**——兩邊共用一個履約價 $K$ 與一個到期日 $T$。在 $t_c$ 持有人取 $\\max(c, p)$，而買賣權平價把它變成一個買權加上一個寫在*遠期價*上的賣權，於是得到一個由兩個單變量常態組成的封閉解（`analyticsimplechooserengine.cpp:74-87`）："

#: ../../maths/exotics.md:230 4cad98a124cd48c9afb2c36640d8d7d0
#, python-brace-format
msgid ""
"W = S D_q(T)\\,N(d) - K D_r(T)\\,N\\big(d - \\sigma\\sqrt{T}\\big)\n"
"- S D_q(T)\\,N(-y) + K D_r(T)\\,N\\big(-y + \\sigma\\sqrt{t_c}\\big),"
msgstr ""

#: ../../maths/exotics.md:233 852ec0c4a021423da9b3c8a0e75a0711
msgid ""
"d = \\frac{\\ln(S/K) + \\big(b + \\tfrac{1}{2}\\sigma^2\\big)T}{\\sigma\\sqrt{T}},\n"
"\\qquad\n"
"y = \\frac{\\ln(S/K) + bT + \\tfrac{1}{2}\\sigma^2 t_c}{\\sigma\\sqrt{t_c}}."
msgstr ""

#: ../../maths/exotics.md:237 869d686e7be94717b3e284799f7f6c53
msgid "The first two terms are a call struck $K$ at $T$; the second two are a put on what is left, and they carry $t_c$ rather than $T$ because the choice is made then."
msgstr "前兩項是一個履約價 $K$、到期 $T$ 的買權；後兩項是寫在剩下那部分上的賣權，而它們帶的是 $t_c$ 而不是 $T$，因為選擇就是在那時候做的。"

#: ../../maths/exotics.md:241 595f5ab6524c47889fa8833101b6be85
msgid "**Complex chooser** — the two sides have strikes and expiries of their own, $(X_c, T_c)$ and $(X_p, T_p)$. Parity no longer applies, so the holder's rule becomes a critical spot again: the $I$ at which the call and the put are worth the same at $t_c$,"
msgstr "**複雜選擇者**——兩邊各有自己的履約價與到期日，$(X_c, T_c)$ 與 $(X_p, T_p)$。平價關係不再適用，所以持有人的決策規則又變成一個臨界現貨價：在 $t_c$ 讓買權與賣權價值相等的那個 $I$，"

#: ../../maths/exotics.md:246 3750fec9332f49efb3246f7049e35ba1
msgid "c\\big(I, X_c, T_c\\big) = p\\big(I, X_p, T_p\\big),"
msgstr ""

#: ../../maths/exotics.md:248 ca2713e846f54d90ae24a5249b291be3
#, python-brace-format
msgid "found by Newton-Raphson, after which the price is four bivariate normal terms with $\\rho_c = \\sqrt{t_c/T_c}$ and $\\rho_p = \\sqrt{t_c/T_p}$ (`analyticcomplexchooserengine.cpp:38-72`)."
msgstr "以 Newton-Raphson 法求出，之後價格就是四個雙變量常態項，相關係數為 $\\rho_c = \\sqrt{t_c/T_c}$ 與 $\\rho_p = \\sqrt{t_c/T_p}$（`analyticcomplexchooserengine.cpp:38-72`）。"

#: ../../maths/exotics.md:252 95e95333b8b349b2be4d470870a1f364
msgid "That solver is where the one bound worth knowing comes from. QuantLib runs its inner Black-Scholes calculation to $T - 2t_c$ rather than $T - t_c$ (`analyticcomplexchooserengine.cpp:91,99`), so a leg expiring inside twice the choice date leaves it a negative time to work with. The service refuses that rather than letting the volatility surface throw from inside the iteration."
msgstr "那個求解器正是唯一一條值得知道的界線的來源。QuantLib 內層的 Black-Scholes 計算跑到的是 $T - 2t_c$ 而不是 $T - t_c$（`analyticcomplexchooserengine.cpp:91,99`），所以某一腳如果在選擇日的兩倍之內就到期，就會留給它一個負的時間。服務會拒絕這種情況，而不是讓波動率曲面在迭代裡面拋出例外。"

#: ../../maths/exotics.md:258 64e866d917a04a6698520b3d602d6a98
msgid "Basket"
msgstr "一籃子"

#: ../../maths/exotics.md:260 3891590bc9f848209d8416159647e994
msgid "Two or more assets, accumulated to one number and handed to a plain payoff. Which accumulation you choose is not a flavour of one formula — it decides which formula exists at all."
msgstr "兩個以上的資產，先累加成一個數字，再交給底下那個一般型收益函數。你選哪一種累加方式，並不是同一條公式的不同口味——它決定的是究竟有沒有公式可用。"

#: ../../maths/exotics.md:264 a77f309655ff4be4a7e19a86b3a43b27
#, python-brace-format
msgid "**Minimum and maximum**, two assets, are Stulz (1982). The whole engine is *one* closed form and two identities. The one form is the call on the minimum: with $\\sigma_i$ the standard deviations $\\sigma_i\\sqrt{T}$, $F_i$ the forwards, and"
msgstr "**最小值與最大值**，兩個資產，走的是 Stulz（1982）。整個引擎就只有*一條*封閉解加上兩條恆等式。那一條就是寫在最小值上的買權：其中 $\\sigma_i$ 是標準差 $\\sigma_i\\sqrt{T}$，$F_i$ 是遠期價，並令"

#: ../../maths/exotics.md:269 c869f2c429384068b792441569c658af
msgid ""
"\\sigma^2 = \\sigma_1^2 + \\sigma_2^2 - 2\\rho\\sigma_1\\sigma_2, \\qquad\n"
"d = \\frac{\\ln(F_1/F_2) + \\tfrac{1}{2}\\sigma^2}{\\sigma},"
msgstr ""

#: ../../maths/exotics.md:272 c4a19a941fa049998d7f9a51893b4a33
#, python-brace-format
msgid ""
"c_{\\min} = D_r\\Big[F_1 M\\big(d_1^{(1)}, -d;\\ \\rho_1'\\big)\n"
"+ F_2 M\\big(d_1^{(2)},\\ d - \\sigma;\\ \\rho_2'\\big)\n"
"- K\\,M\\big(d_1^{(1)} - \\sigma_1,\\ d_1^{(2)} - \\sigma_2;\\ \\rho\\big)\\Big],"
msgstr ""

#: ../../maths/exotics.md:276 d06d21b914fa4860b9a6ff1538f07565
msgid "where $\\rho_1' = (\\rho\\sigma_2 - \\sigma_1)/\\sigma$ and $\\rho_2' = (\\rho\\sigma_1 - \\sigma_2)/\\sigma$. Note that $\\sigma$ is the volatility of the *ratio* of the two assets — the minimum is a question about which one is smaller, and that is a question about the ratio."
msgstr "其中 $\\rho_1' = (\\rho\\sigma_2 - \\sigma_1)/\\sigma$、$\\rho_2' = (\\rho\\sigma_1 - \\sigma_2)/\\sigma$。注意 $\\sigma$ 是兩個資產*比值*的波動率——取最小值問的是哪一個比較小，而那正是一個關於比值的問題。"

#: ../../maths/exotics.md:281 3f8e89ece7aa4154b22c59f7900c70d0
#, python-brace-format
msgid "The two identities do the rest. A call on the maximum is $c_{\\max} = c_1 + c_2 - c_{\\min}$, because $\\max + \\min = a + b$ (`stulzengine.cpp:63-79`). And each put comes from parity against a zero-strike call, which is the accumulation itself:"
msgstr "其餘的由那兩條恆等式完成。寫在最大值上的買權是 $c_{\\max} = c_1 + c_2 - c_{\\min}$，因為 $\\max + \\min = a + b$（`stulzengine.cpp:63-79`）。而每一個賣權都來自與零履約價買權之間的平價關係，而那個零履約價買權就是累加本身："

#: ../../maths/exotics.md:286 5d93c4ed1f724f6fb0dd06501f232a18
msgid "p = K D_r - c(K = 0) + c(K)."
msgstr ""

#: ../../maths/exotics.md:288 e6952addd30c40f9b752b8126cd727a2
msgid "QuantLib's own source carries a warning here worth passing on: the line that discounts the dividend yields is commented *\"cannot handle non zero dividends, so don't believe this\"* (`stulzengine.cpp:129`). It is more cautious than the evidence — four of the reference rows this build prices carry dividend yields of 6% and 9% and reproduce Haug's published values to 1e-4 — but it is the library's own doubt about its own formula, and worth knowing before you trust a dividend-paying basket further than the table goes."
msgstr "QuantLib 自己的原始碼在這裡帶著一句值得轉達的警告：折現股利收益率的那一行旁邊寫著 *\"cannot handle non zero dividends, so don't believe this\"*（`stulzengine.cpp:129`）。它比證據所顯示的更保守——這個版本計價的參考列裡，有四列帶著 6% 與 9% 的股利收益率，而且都把 Haug 公布的值重現到 1e-4——但那畢竟是函式庫對自己公式的懷疑，在你把配息一籃子信任到超出那張表的範圍之前，值得先知道。"

#: ../../maths/exotics.md:296 1be37ff874ff4a52825e640d409ad81e
msgid "**Spread**, two assets, is Kirk, and it is the most economical trick on this page. A spread call pays $\\max(S_1 - S_2 - K, 0)$, which is not lognormal in anything. Kirk treats $F_2 + K$ as if it were, which turns the whole trade into a *single* Black call on the ratio:"
msgstr "**價差**，兩個資產，走的是 Kirk，而它是本頁最經濟的一個技巧。價差買權支付 $\\max(S_1 - S_2 - K, 0)$，而這對任何東西都不是對數常態的。Kirk 把 $F_2 + K$ 當成是對數常態的，於是整筆交易就變成寫在比值上的*單一*一個 Black 買權："

#: ../../maths/exotics.md:301 79cc4e04fb9e480c951be6ae62f7f4a2
msgid ""
"F = \\frac{F_1}{F_2 + K}, \\qquad\n"
"\\sigma_{\\text{eff}}^2 = \\sigma_1^2\n"
"+ \\sigma_2^2\\left(\\frac{F_2}{F_2+K}\\right)^2\n"
"- 2\\rho\\,\\sigma_1\\sigma_2\\left(\\frac{F_2}{F_2+K}\\right),"
msgstr ""

#: ../../maths/exotics.md:306 b9bfb34bfe03455886ef9efa2522ede0
msgid "V = (F_2 + K)\\; \\text{Black}\\big(F,\\ 1,\\ \\sigma_{\\text{eff}},\\ D_r\\big)."
msgstr ""

#: ../../maths/exotics.md:308 193f649d771940a4839bd617ba72573a
msgid "At $K = 0$ the weight $F_2/(F_2+K)$ is 1 and $\\sigma_{\\text{eff}}$ is exactly the ratio's volatility — the approximation vanishes and Kirk is Margrabe's exchange option. It degrades as $K$ grows relative to $F_2$ (`kirkengine.cpp:35-49`)."
msgstr "當 $K = 0$ 時，權重 $F_2/(F_2+K)$ 等於 1，而 $\\sigma_{\\text{eff}}$ 恰好就是比值的波動率——近似消失，Kirk 就是 Margrabe 的交換選擇權。$K$ 相對於 $F_2$ 越大，它就退化得越厲害（`kirkengine.cpp:35-49`）。"

#: ../../maths/exotics.md:313 05b959be30834e9b9d8d9181f7fbefd4
#, python-brace-format
msgid "**Everything else is Monte Carlo.** A weighted average has no closed form here, and neither does any basket of three or more assets. The assets are evolved together through a `StochasticProcessArray`, which factorises the correlation matrix once and drives the whole system off one set of correlated normals. That factorisation is why the matrix has to be positive semi-definite, and why this build checks that it is: given one that is not, QuantLib repairs it rather than refusing it ({doc}`../market`)."
msgstr "**其餘一律走蒙地卡羅**。加權平均在這裡沒有封閉解，三個以上資產的一籃子也沒有。這些資產是透過 `StochasticProcessArray` 一起演化的：它把相關係數矩陣分解一次，然後用一組相關的常態亂數推動整個系統。正是那個分解，使得矩陣必須是半正定的，也正是這個版本要去檢查它的原因——因為給它一個不是半正定的矩陣，QuantLib 會把它修好，而不是拒絕它（{doc}`../market`）。"

#: ../../maths/exotics.md:321 b82738ddee574c0abc245b6545b763e3
msgid "One-touch digitals"
msgstr "One-touch 二元選擇權"

#: ../../maths/exotics.md:323 74ef2869f94b4ed5a0941e188feb3320
msgid "A binary payoff on an *American* exercise is a one-touch: it pays as soon as the level is reached rather than at expiry, and it goes to QuantLib's digital American engine. Its value is exactly the $F$ term of the barrier formula above — a rebate paid at hit — which is the cleanest way to remember what a one-touch is: the rebate of a knock-out, sold on its own."
msgstr "*美式*履約上的二元收益函數就是 one-touch：它在水準被觸及的當下就給付，而不是等到到期，並且會走 QuantLib 的二元美式引擎。它的價值恰好就是上面障礙公式中的 $F$ 項——觸及時支付的回饋金——這也是記住 one-touch 是什麼的最乾淨方式：把敲出選擇權的回饋金單獨拿出來賣。"

#: ../../maths/exotics.md:329 b82738ddee574c0abc245b6545b763e3
msgid "Knock digitals"
msgstr "敲出入二元選擇權"

#: ../../maths/exotics.md:331 41abefa796ae42c49c6bf8b1f14c90ca
msgid "The same binary payoff on a **barrier** is a different trade and a different engine: it pays a fixed amount, or the asset, at expiry, but only if the barrier was touched (*in*) or was not (*out*). This is the trade the schema's `digital` style names, and it has no instrument of its own in QuantLib — the shape *is* the product."
msgstr "同樣的二元收益函數放在**障礙**上，是另一筆交易、另一個引擎：它在到期日支付一筆固定金額或標的資產，但前提是障礙曾被觸及（*in*）或未曾被觸及（*out*）。這就是結構描述裡 `digital` 類型所指的交易，而它在 QuantLib 裡沒有自己的商品類別——這個組合*就是*那個商品。"

#: ../../maths/exotics.md:337 53fca96969954712a589caaef0979baf
msgid "The formula is the barrier assembly at the top of this page with the vanilla payoff swapped out, which is why the two look so alike:"
msgstr "公式就是本頁最上方那組障礙選擇權的組裝，只是把一般型收益函數換掉，這也是為什麼兩者看起來如此相像："

#: ../../maths/exotics.md:340 2877fed6fa4b4ead9c5e750cb159257f
msgid ""
"x_1 = \\frac{\\ln(S/K)}{v} + \\mu v, \\qquad\n"
"x_2 = \\frac{\\ln(S/H)}{v} + \\mu v, \\qquad\n"
"y_1 = \\frac{\\ln\\!\\big(H^2/SK\\big)}{v} + \\mu v, \\qquad\n"
"y_2 = \\frac{\\ln(H/S)}{v} + \\mu v,"
msgstr ""

#: ../../maths/exotics.md:345 f165a0a8c839465aa223d63180b941e3
#, python-brace-format
msgid "with $\\mu = \\ln\\!\\big(D_q/D_r\\big)/\\sigma^2 T - \\tfrac{1}{2}$. Sixteen cases fall out of four barrier types × two payoff kinds × call or put — Haug's pp. 176–180, and the sixteen rows this build prices as two reference tables."
msgstr "其中 $\\mu = \\ln\\!\\big(D_q/D_r\\big)/\\sigma^2 T - \\tfrac{1}{2}$。四種障礙型態 × 兩種二元收益函數 × 買權或賣權，總共落出十六種情況——Haug 第 176–180 頁，也就是這個版本以兩張參考表計價的那十六列。"

#: ../../maths/exotics.md:349 8d3cb2a673114d2abbeb0558285e7bb5
msgid "The one thing worth carrying away is how little separates the two payoffs. A cash-or-nothing pays $K$; an asset-or-nothing pays the asset, and in the engine that is exactly $\\mu \\to \\mu + 1$ with the cash amount replaced by the forward (`analyticbinarybarrierengine.cpp:65-72`). The same six terms, one shift of the drift."
msgstr "唯一值得記住的一點，是這兩種收益函數之間的差別有多小。現金或零支付 $K$；資產或零支付標的資產，而在引擎裡這恰好就是 $\\mu \\to \\mu + 1$，再把現金金額換成遠期價（`analyticbinarybarrierengine.cpp:65-72`）。同樣的六項，只是漂移項挪了一格。"

#: ../../maths/exotics.md:355 eccf1958c55c414fb653c4558de08252
msgid "Two branches never reach the formula. An **out** option whose spot is already past the barrier is worth nothing, with every greek zero. An **in** option whose spot is already past it has knocked in, so it is simply a European digital, and QuantLib prices it with the ordinary analytic engine. Both are the honest answer rather than a special case."
msgstr "有兩條分支根本走不到那條公式。現貨價已經越過障礙的 **out** 型選擇權一文不值，所有希臘字母都是零。現貨價已經越過障礙的 **in** 型則已經敲入，所以它就只是一個歐式二元選擇權，QuantLib 用一般的解析解引擎去算。這兩者都是誠實的答案，而不是特例處理。"

#: ../../maths/exotics.md:361 1be2c957e6494b57aeb266541df2e11f
msgid "**No rebate.** The engine never reads one. A rebate sent with a knock digital would have been taken and dropped and a price returned for a different trade, so the service refuses it — the only rule on this page that QuantLib itself would not have raised."
msgstr "**沒有回饋金**。引擎根本不會去讀它。跟著敲出入二元選擇權一起送來的回饋金，會被收下、丟棄，然後回給你另一筆交易的價格，所以服務會拒絕它——這是本頁唯一一條 QuantLib 自己不會提出來的規則。"

